  nodeAbstract: 
  nodeTextLayers:
  - Here you can see insulin monomers group into dimers, and then form a hexamer,
    the basic subunit of the insulin crystal.
  - The hexamer formation process is dependent on the zinc concentration in the insulin
    vesicle.
  - The kinetics of insulin oligerization has great discrepancies in studies, however
    it is believed that hexamer formation is about 100x slower than dimerization.
